---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const path = '/privacy/';
const updated = '21 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Next Scale Digital"
  description="What Next Scale Digital collects when you use this website or contact us, why, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted."
  path={path}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', href: path }]}
>
  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="wrap-tight">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-tight legal">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static website. It does not set advertising cookies, it does not
        build a profile of you, and it does not sell anything to anyone. If you fill
        in the contact form, the details go to us so we can reply to you, and that
        is all they are used for.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you contact us.</strong> The name, business name, email address,
        phone number, website address, service area and message you type into the form
        on the contact page, or send to us by email.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>When you browse.</strong> Standard server logs held by our host, which
        include IP address, browser type and the pages requested. If website analytics
        are running, they record aggregate visit data. We do not use analytics to
        identify individual people.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
      <p>
        To reply to your enquiry, to run any audit you have asked for, and to deliver
        services if you become a client. We do not use your details for unrelated
        marketing, we do not add you to a mailing list without you asking, and we do
        not sell or rent them to anybody.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p>
        Our email provider and our website host, as a necessary part of delivering
        the message and serving the page. If you become a client, the platforms
        needed to do the work, such as Google Ads or Google Search Console, using
        accounts held in your name.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will disclose information where the law requires it. Otherwise, no.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become work are deleted within two years. Client
        records are held for as long as the engagement runs and for seven years
        afterwards, which is the period Canadian business records are normally
        retained for.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Canadian privacy law you can ask what personal information we hold about
        you, ask for it to be corrected, and ask for it to be deleted. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will action it within
        thirty days.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies of its own. Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts,
        which means your browser makes a request to Google&rsquo;s servers when a page
        loads. If analytics are enabled, they may set a first-party cookie to
        distinguish repeat visits. Nothing here is used for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Material changes
        affecting existing clients will be sent by email rather than left here to be
        discovered.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about any of this go to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We are based in {site.city},
        {site.regionName}, {site.countryName}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-hero { background: var(--ink); color: var(--fg-on-ink); padding-block: var(--sp-7); }
  .legal-hero .eyebrow { color: var(--brand-lite); }
  .legal-hero .eyebrow::after { background: var(--rule-dark); }
  .legal-hero h1 { color: var(--paper); font-size: var(--step-3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .legal-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--fg-faint); margin: 0; }

  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
</style>
